omggif is a JavaScript implementation of a GIF 89a encoder and decoder.

https://github.com/deanm/omggif


Decoding semantics (explicit, not guessed)
------------------------------------------

- `GifReader` exposes the indexed-frame API (`frameInfo`,
  `decodeAndBlitFrameRGBA/BGRA`) and `GifCompositor` provides logical-canvas
  compositing: `compositeFrame(n)` returns the full RGBA canvas as it should
  be displayed while frame n is shown.
- A Graphics Control Extension applies to exactly one frame.  A frame
  without its own GCE gets the defaults: delay 0, no transparency,
  disposal 0 ("no disposal specified", composited as "leave in place").
- `loopCount()` returns `null` when the file has no Netscape looping block,
  meaning "play once".  Only an explicit block yields a number
  (0 = loop forever).
- Disposal: 0/1 (and reserved 4-7) leave the canvas in place; 2 clears the
  frame's rectangle to transparent; 3 restores the canvas to what it was
  before that frame.  A frame's disposal is applied when advancing past it.
  Transparent pixels never overwrite the canvas below them.
- Frames extending outside the logical screen are clipped by
  `GifCompositor`; the raw `decodeAndBlitFrame*` API rejects them instead.
- `compositeFrame(n)` is idempotent: repeated calls for the same frame
  return the same canvas and never accumulate on the cached state.
- Stable errors are raised before any pixel is written when a frame
  rectangle does not fit the logical screen, when a palette index is out of
  range, or when a frame has no color table.  Truncated extensions raise
  stable parse errors.


Tests
-----

The test suite uses offline minimal GIF fixtures (test/fixtures/, generated
by test/gen_fixtures.js) and an independent per-pixel compositing reference
(test/reference.js) that shares no code with omggif.js.  Assertions are on
decoded canvas pixels and frame metadata, covering disposal 0/1/2/3,
missing/local palettes, transparent edges, out-of-canvas frames, truncated
extensions, interlaced pass order, and repeated compositor reuse.

    node test/gen_fixtures.js   # regenerate fixtures (already committed)
    node test/run_tests.js      # run the suite


